1. The tracking efficiency in Au+Au is \(90\%\pm 7\%\) of that in _p+p_ for \(p_{\rm T}>2\) GeV/\(c\) (see Appendix A). In order to reflect this in the _p+p_ HT \(\otimes\) Au+Au MB embedding, 10% of the tracks in the _p+p_ event are randomly rejected before calculating \(p_{\rm T}^{p+p,{\rm emb}}\). In order to calculate the systematic uncertainty bands corresponding to the uncertainty on the tracking efficiency, the _p+p_ HT \(\otimes\) Au+Au MB embedding is redone with 17% and 3% of the tracks being rejected, and the extracted Gaussian yields (\(Y_{\rm NS}\) and \(Y_{\rm AS}\)) are also adjusted to account for the possible variation in tracking efficiency.
2. The tower efficiency in Au+Au is \(98\%\pm 2\%\) that in _p+p_. In order to reflect

