4. In each event, the full FTPC event plane is the weighted average of the shifted sub-event planes: \[\Psi_{2,\rm full}=\frac{1}{2}\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{|Q_{2,\rm west}|\sin(2\Psi_ {2,\rm west})+|Q_{2,\rm east}|\sin(2\Psi_{2,\rm east})}{|Q_{2,\rm west}|\cos( 2\Psi_{2,\rm west})+|Q_{2,\rm east}|\cos(2\Psi_{2,\rm east})}\right)\] (5.8)
5. The distribution of full event planes is flattened by shifting.

Recentering and shifting are done on a run-by-run basis. Figure 5.4 shows the distribution of the event planes after each step in the procedure described above.

